<p>The  was a major religious, political, and military endeavour of the , usually dated from the 1095 . There  proclaimed the  in support of  under Muslim rule, framing it as a form of penitential . The crusaders founded  in the , the defence of which inspired further . The  later launched campaigns against Muslims in ,  in the Baltic, and other opponents of its authority. Core crusading forces were heavily armed , backed by infantry, local troops, and naval aid from maritime cities. These papal-sanctioned wars fostered distinctive institutions and ideologies. Funding was initially improvised, but later supported via  and the sale of . The fusion of chivalric and monastic ideals led to the rise of . The movement extended  and left lasting marks on art and literature. 
