<p>The  was a two-ship  of  built for the  (IJN) in the mid-1890s. They were the first battleships in the IJN, and were constructed in the United Kingdom as Japan lacked the industrial facilities needed to build them. The ships participated in the  of 1904–1905, including the  in February 1904 and two bombardments of  the following month.  struck a  off Port Arthur in May and  while under tow several hours later.   fought in the  and the , and was lightly damaged in the latter action. She was reclassified as a  in 1910 and served as a  for the rest of her active career.  was  in 1922, converted into a  fitted with classrooms, and was finally  for scrap in 1948. 
