<p>The  was organized in June 1776 as a  unit of riflemen in the  during the . The  consisted of nine  — four from Maryland and five from Virginia and was directly responsible to national authority as an . Most of the regiment surrendered to British and German forces at the  on November 16, 1776. However, a portion of the unit continued to serve actively in the Continental Army throughout most of the remainder of the war. Elements of the regiment served with 's main army and participated in its major engagements. Select members of the unit were also attached to Colonal 's elite . The regiment was reorganized in January 1779 and stationed at , headquarters of the Continental Army's , in present-day western . Disbanded in January 1781, it was the longest serving Continental Army rifle unit of the war. 
